  "notes": "TLC-mentored girl trio — Left Eye's protégées, 1999–2002. The research gives \"61–109; half-time ballads 61–64, straight uptempos 89–109\", and the half-time band is encoded because it is the only band the entry describes as a kit: the title track, \"named for the **TR-808** and built on it, kick on 1, 808 clap on beat 3, 808 cowbell/hat ornament\". So the band is narrow (61–64, mode 61 — the sourced reading), `halfTime` is true and the snare is `halftime_3`. Three drum deltas: a kick at one or two hits a bar with `lockTo808` 0.5 and syncopation 0.05, a clap stacked on beat 3 within 2 ms and `offGridMs` 0, and a cowbell-led perc pair at −6 dB with a hat lane at 0.12 fill density. This is a true 808 model — \"808 sub-bass on the vamp root with long decay on the title track\" — so `drums.bass808` carries role `bassline` and there is no `bassline` block; the entry also notes \"sampled bass on the pop-crossover cuts\", which belongs to the straight band that is not modelled here. Harmony is \"two-chord minor vamps\". \"Three-part harmony in a TLC-derived narrow stack (unison-plus-third rather than wide gospel spread), rap-adjacent rhythmic verses, sung hook of 4–5 pitches\" is the 0.82 step share, the riff-dominant contour and the 4–5 pitch motif. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ Every velocity, density and portamento number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode ballads, major-mode pop-crossover uptempos [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line. ⚠ **`chords.harmonicRhythm` re-weighted (2026-08-17, harmony variety floor).** The entry's harmony line is \"two-chord minor vamps, three-part harmony in a TLC-derived narrow stack\", and the engine's `vamp` value is *one* chord held for the whole clip (`generators::chords`: \"One chord for the whole pattern\") — so weighting `vamp` at the top rendered a **one**-chord bed the research nowhere describes. The chord motion the entry states is now carried by `1_per_bar` (the pair over a 2-bar cell) and `2_bars_per_chord` (the pair over a 4-bar cell), with `vamp` kept as the minority for the held reading. ⚠ The split between those two rates is **INFERRED** — the entry names the device, not its rate.",
